|~ `::law`, the kind of a law, and the laws declared under it.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence], [QSSLF#laws]. ~|

:law
  |~~ A law is a claim about a name that runs: a query that answers
      true, a quote under this tag laid under the name whose behaviour it
      proves, its page the sentence of the claim. The chain of a function
      or a kind writes it by `proves`,
      `| proves :addsTheNumber |~~ Ten and three is thirteen. ~~| ~(10 | add 3 | eq 13)`,
      as `holds` writes an invariant, a quote under `::invariant`, and a
      law of any other name, a label among them, is declared under it,
      `:Box/holdsItsWidth ::law~(::Box{:width 1} | get /width | eq 1);`.
      A law is code held as data: it reads the verbs of the tree and the names it
      declares, and no value the reader named, and a law of a name the
      language declares runs over the root alone.

      `laws` answers the laws of a name, each its page and its query,
      and `runLaws` runs them, so the examples of the catalog are its
      tests.
      ::link~(::any/laws) ::link~(::any/runLaws)
      ::link~(::invariant) ::link~(::qlang/hypertext)
      ::link~(::qlang/code)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | accepts |~~ The query that proves the claim, a quote. ~~| ::quote
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ A law is a quote that answers true, `::law~(3 | eq 3)`, which
            `proves` writes in a chain; a quote under another tag gives the
            quote beneath by `payload`.
        ~~|
    | proves :provesItsClaim
        |~~ A law declared under a name proves its claim when it runs. ~~|
        ~(:Box |~~ A box. ~~|; :Box/holdsItsWidth |~~ A box holds its width. ~~| ::law~(::Box{:width 1} | get /width | eq 1); ::Box | runLaws | map /ok | eq [true])
    | proves :readsNoValueOfTheReader
        |~~ A law reads no value the reader named. ~~|
        ~({:limit 5} | with [/limit] (:Box |~~ A box. ~~|; :Box/withinTheLimit |~~ The limit is five. ~~| ::law~(limit | eq 5); ::Box | runLaws | first | get /error | tag) | eq ::call/ValueWithheldError)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesANumber
        |~~ A law is a quote. ~~|
        ~(::law#3 !| tag | eq ::law/PayloadKindNotTakenError)
    | proves :holdsAQuoteByItsOwnTag
        |~~ The query of a law is a quote, a quote under another tag refused.
        ~~|
        ~(::law::Foo~(3 | eq 3) !| get [tag (found | tag)] | eq [::law/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::Foo]);

